---
import Layout from "../../components/Layout.astro";
import DocShell from "../../components/DocShell.astro";
import CommandBlock from "../../components/CommandBlock.astro";
import SafetyNotice from "../../components/SafetyNotice.astro";
---

<Layout title="ArkheionX Documentation" description="Documentation for ArkheionX local-first Solidity and Foundry review infrastructure.">
  <DocShell>
    <p class="page-kicker">Documentation</p>
    <h1>Build a review surface you can regenerate.</h1>
    <p class="doc-deck">
      ArkheionX reads an authorized local repository and produces structured artifacts for protocol orientation,
      evidence tracking, and review handoff.
    </p>

    <CommandBlock command="curl -fsSL https://arkheionx.dev/install | bash" title="install / main" />

    <h2>Choose a path</h2>
    <div class="definition-grid">
      <div><dt><a href="/docs/getting-started">Getting started</a></dt><dd>Understand the install, first run, and output locations.</dd></div>
      <div><dt><a href="/docs/review-workflow">Review workflow</a></dt><dd>Move from repository orientation to a local review package.</dd></div>
      <div><dt><a href="/docs/concepts">Concepts</a></dt><dd>Roles, value paths, assumptions, gaps, evidence links, and packages.</dd></div>
      <div><dt><a href="/docs/cli-reference">CLI reference</a></dt><dd>Commands, execution boundaries, and output behavior.</dd></div>
    </div>

    <h2>Default operating model</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Analysis starts from files on the local machine.</li>
      <li>Generated artifacts are written under <code>.arkheionx/out/</code>.</li>
      <li>Network and remote-chain access are not required for the default review-map workflow.</li>
      <li>Commands that can invoke Foundry require an explicit execution flag.</li>
      <li>Machine output remains review context until a human validates it against source and evidence.</li>
    </ul>

    <SafetyNotice />
  </DocShell>
</Layout>
